 ## Overview
-The Amanatides–Woo algorithm efficiently enumerates the uniform grid cells intersected by a ray in front-to-back order by jumping exactly from one grid boundary to the next, avoiding the pitfalls of naïve ray marching such as missing thin cells, redundant work, and arbitrary step sizes [S1, S2]. It serves as the foundational traversal method for image-order volume rendering and voxel-based ray casting, building on [Ray-grid traversal](17-ray-grid-traversal.md) by providing an output-sensitive $O(K)$ approach where $K$ is the number of visited cells [S1].
