 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(K)$, where $K$ is the number of visited cells. The algorithm performs constant work per crossed voxel and does not inspect untouched cells [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary space, storing only a few vectors per ray [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Extremely fast per-voxel update (a few comparisons and one addition); output-sensitive; robust for uniform grids [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Only suitable for uniform grids; performance degrades if the ray traverses many empty cells (though better than marching); requires careful handling of ties and boundaries [S1].
-*   **When to use:** Volume rendering, voxel-based collision detection, and any scenario requiring efficient traversal of a uniform spatial grid [S1, S2].
-*   **When not to use:** Non-uniform grids (use hierarchical methods like [Hierarchical Traversal](896-hierarchical-traversal.md) or [HDDA](1122-hierarchical-digital-differential-analyzer-hdda.md)), or when sparse data structures are preferred [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(K)$, where $K$ is the number of visited cells. The algorithm performs constant work per crossed voxel and does not inspect untouched cells [S1, unofficial].
