 ## Background
-The algorithm was introduced by John Amanatides and Andrew Woo in the paper "A Fast Voxel Traversal Algorithm for Ray Tracing," published at Eurographics in 1987 [S1]. It is a classic example of transforming continuous ray geometry into a discrete event sequence, optimizing the inner loop for ray tracing performance [S1]. It is widely used in voxel engines, medical imaging (e.g., CT reconstruction), and real-time graphics [S2, S3].
